[00:30.68] I was standin' by the road in Black Jack County
[00:37.24] Not knowing that the Sheriff paid a bounty
[00:44.19] For men like me who didn't have a penny to their name
[00:51.12] He locked my legs in 35 pounds of Black Jack County chains
[00:59.94] All we had to eat was bread and water
[01:05.99] Every day we had to build his road, a mile and a quarter
[01:13.55] A black snake whip would sting our backs
[01:16.73] If some poor fool complained
[01:20.03] But we couldn't fight back wearin' 35 pounds of Black Jack County chains
[01:27.64] 
[01:57.38] And one night the Sheriff laid sleepin'
[02:05.75] We all gathered 'round him, slowly creepin'
[02:13.15] Heaven help me to forget that night in the cold, cold rain
[02:19.77] When we beat him to death wearin' 35 pounds of Black Jack County chains
[02:26.40] 
[02:31.52] The wounds have all healed and I'm thankful
[02:38.51] And there's nothin' left but scars around my ankle
[02:45.51] The best of all, no man will ever be a slave again
[02:52.64] To a black snake whip and 35 pounds of Black Jack County chains
[03:01.86] Best of all, no man will ever be a slave again
